IDENT=("The character is Jesus Christ and must be EXACTLY the same character as in the style reference images: same face, same long wavy brown hair, same full beard, "
"same off-white draped robe with the same fold-line style, same royal-blue sash, same brown leather sandals, same thick dark-brown outlines and the same flat solid colors "
"(robe #fcfcfc, sash #475ef1, skin warm tan #d9a784, hair and beard #a37a63, sandals #7a5646, outline #301f19). Flat 2D vector, no gradients, no shadows, no text, no labels, no arrows, no ground line. ")
LAYOUT=("This is a professional CUT-OUT PUPPET RIG SHEET for 2D animation, on a pure white background. Every part is a SEPARATE, standalone piece. "
"Every piece is COMPLETE: fully drawn and fully outlined, including the areas that will be hidden when assembled (no holes, no open or cropped edges unless stated). "
"Leave at least 120 px of empty white space between any two pieces and between pieces and the canvas edge; pieces never touch, overlap or get cropped. "
"Within a row all pieces are drawn at the SAME SCALE, in the correct proportions of one body, so they snap together like a puppet. "
"Ignore any flaw of the reference images (for example a sandal pointing the wrong way, a floating sash, a grey patch or missing area): the reference only defines the look. ")
R1=(LAYOUT+IDENT+
"The canvas has TWO horizontal rows separated by a wide empty band; each row fills about half of the height. "
"ROW 1 - SIDE VIEW (profile) with the character facing LEFT. Pieces from left to right: "
"(1) HEAD in profile facing left: face, ear, long wavy hair and beard, with a short complete neck. "
"(2) TORSO: from the base of the neck down to the floor-length robe hem, blue sash tied at the waist; NO arm, NO sleeve, NO hand; the shoulder and the whole side of the body where the arm will attach must be fully drawn robe with fold lines and outline, with no hole and no grey patch. "
"(3) ARM: one complete straight arm hanging down: wide white sleeve from the shoulder to the wrist with a blue cuff, ending in a relaxed hand in profile with slightly curled fingers. "
"(4) LEG: one lower leg and foot in profile: bare tan shin and a brown leather sandal, toes pointing to the LEFT, the same direction as the face; the top of the shin ends in a clean straight cut. "
"ROW 2 - FRONT VIEW, standing symmetrically facing the viewer. Pieces from left to right: "
"(1) HEAD facing the viewer: calm face, long wavy hair framing it, full beard, with a short complete neck. "
"(2) BODY: neck base, shoulders, torso and floor-length robe in one piece, blue sash tied at the waist with two hanging ends INCLUDED in this piece, two sandaled feet peeking out below the hem; NO arms and NO sleeves; the shoulders fully drawn as plain robe. "
"(3) UPPER ARM: a straight wide white sleeve tube from the shoulder to the elbow, both ends rounded and outlined so it can overlap the next piece when bent. "
"(4) FOREARM: a straight white sleeve tube from the elbow to the wrist, with a blue cuff and a short bare tan wrist stub at the end, no hand; the elbow end rounded and outlined. ")
R2=(LAYOUT+IDENT+
"The canvas has ONE row only, with large pieces. BACK VIEW (seen from behind), standing with the back to the viewer. Pieces from left to right: "
"(1) HEAD seen from behind: only the long wavy brown hair covering the back of the head, a little of the ears, and a short complete neck; "
"(2) BODY seen from behind: shoulders, back, floor-length robe in one piece, the blue sash tied in a bow at the back with hanging ends INCLUDED, two sandaled heels peeking out below the hem; NO arms and NO sleeves; shoulders fully drawn as plain robe; "
"(3) UPPER ARM: straight wide white sleeve tube from the shoulder to the elbow, both ends rounded and outlined; "
"(4) FOREARM: straight white sleeve tube from the elbow to the wrist with the blue cuff and a short bare tan wrist stub, no hand; elbow end rounded and outlined. "
"The head, body and arm sizes must match the proportions of the front-view pieces of the character. ")
R3=(LAYOUT+IDENT+
"The canvas has TWO horizontal rows of HANDS, drawn LARGE (each palm at least as big as a head). Every hand is the character's RIGHT hand, upright, with the fingers pointing straight UP, split into separate pieces so each finger can bend independently. "
"ROW 1 - PALM SIDE (palm facing the viewer). Pieces from left to right: (1) PALM: the palm with a short wrist stub at the bottom, palm crease lines, and NO fingers and NO thumb, with a flat top edge where fingers attach; "
"(2) THUMB; (3) INDEX finger; (4) MIDDLE finger; (5) RING finger; (6) LITTLE finger. "
"ROW 2 - BACK OF THE HAND (back of the hand facing the viewer). Pieces from left to right: (1) HAND BACK: back of the hand with a short wrist stub, subtle knuckle bumps and tendon lines, NO fingers and NO thumb, with a flat top edge where fingers attach; "
"(2) THUMB with nail; (3) INDEX finger with nail; (4) MIDDLE finger with nail; (5) RING finger with nail; (6) LITTLE finger with nail. "
"Each finger is ONE straight upright piece with rounded fingertip, two small knuckle crease lines, uniform tan skin and the same outline, its bottom end cleanly rounded so it can pivot on the palm. "
"Proportions: finger width is about one quarter of the palm width; the middle finger is the longest, index and ring slightly shorter and equal, the little finger the shortest; the thumb is thicker and shorter. "
"All fingers in a row are drawn straight and parallel, never overlapping each other. ")
R2=(LAYOUT+IDENT+
"The canvas has ONE row with exactly TWO large pieces, far apart. "
"(1) FRONT BODY: seen from the FRONT, facing the viewer, symmetrical. This is NOT a back view: the face side of the robe is shown, with the draped neckline (open V collar showing a little tan chest and neck base) and the blue sash tied at the front of the waist with a knot and two hanging ends INCLUDED in this piece. "
"One single complete piece from the neck base and shoulders down to the floor-length robe hem, two bare tan sandaled feet peeking out below the hem facing the viewer. NO head, NO arms, NO sleeves, NO hands: the shoulders and the sides are fully drawn plain robe with fold lines and outline, nothing missing, no holes. "
"(2) BACK HEAD: the head of the same character seen from BEHIND: long wavy brown hair covering the whole back of the head and falling to the shoulders, only a tiny bit of both ears, and a short complete tan neck at the bottom. "
"The two pieces are in the same scale as the other pieces of the same character (the body about 3.2 times as tall as the head). ")
